The animation will start with a unit circle centered at the origin on the left side of the screen and the graph of y = sin(x) on the right side. A point will move counterclockwise around the unit circle. As the point moves, its y-coordinate will be used to plot the corresponding point on the graph of y = sin(x) on the right side, effectively tracing out the sine wave in synchronization with the point's movement around the circle. The animation will continue until the point completes one full revolution around the unit circle, resulting in a complete tracing of the sine wave from x = 0 to x = 2π.
</final_translation>

